[01:02.913]I know I can't define this life.
[01:05.612]I know you can't see through.
[01:09.228]These answers I'm seeking for
[01:11.956]Are way too deep to be found.
[01:15.573]My life's reflected through the wet film of my eyes.
[01:21.441]I've been betraying the kid that I was.
[01:24.165]Do you think this life really deserves an anthem ?
[01:28.236]I’ve been changing.
[01:30.038]It reminds me when I was younger and useless.
[01:33.658]My heart beats, covered in bruises.
[01:36.785]I saw this room slowly turn to a coffin.
[01:39.506]As locked in, but I'm not dead yet.
[01:43.104]I did my best to show you that I've been changing,
[01:49.925]And what I've been through to see clearly through myself.
[02:11.086]I was such a mess before this,
[02:14.245]I don't miss it, no, I don't miss it.
[02:16.933]My heart has braced itself,
[02:18.719]I'll set this world in check,
[02:20.069]I finally found myself.
[02:23.680]I've got my dreams and all my memories in my head.
[02:28.630]I don't wanna be the one who can live without this.
[02:35.298]All that I can see is the distance since these days.
[02:41.179]I wouldn't recognize myself
[02:43.459]Without the mess of what I've done with my life.
[03:00.683]I will never let you define my way of life.
[03:06.554]I thought we've been watching the same sun
[03:09.278]But we're way too far to finally feel warmed.
[03:13.091]This is my time to speak.
[03:15.704]This is the time to forgive.
[03:18.782]I've been betraying the kid that I was.
[03:21.869]Do you think this life really deserves an anthem ?
[03:40.619]I didn't think the show would last so long.
[03:43.712]Though it should last forever now.
[03:46.822]I was seeking for this ;
[03:48.344]Having a chance to speak to try to feel better.
[03:53.002]I see your face when your eyes are staring back at me.
[03:58.080]I can fake it,
[03:59.624]It's not as hard as it seems
[04:01.978]With the detachment the drug brings.
[04:05.507]I've got these dreams to stand for,
[04:07.052]Got my voice to speak despite the lies around me now
[04:11.346]But this bitter taste that they're leaving
[04:14.076]Won't let me feel anything.
[04:29.707]It reminds me when I was younger and useless.
[04:33.225]My heart beats, covered in bruises.
[04:36.356]I saw this room slowly turn to a coffin.
[04:39.083]As locked in, but I'm not dead yet.
